`,r.jsxs(i.p,{children:["It was a struggle, with a lot of errors related to inconsistent naming across SQL and Firestore databases. Luckily, I found ",r.jsx(i.a,{href:"https://orm.drizzle.team/drizzle-studio/overview",children:"this tool"}),", which lets me visualize the local SQL database as I use the app, so I could spot inconsistencies. But eventually, I finished the sync function, which pushes and pulls and handles conflicts when the user is authenticated. Now, users can open the app on a different device and sign in to see all the data from their account restored."]}),`
