`,r.jsx(i.p,{children:"Next, I wanted to explore using an animation library I found called Motion. With this, I can add animations within the JSX, which really simplifies the process of creating animations. I started creating some flip card animations on the main page, which provide a brief description of each subpage and encourage the user to click them."}),`
`,r.jsx(i.p,{children:"I saw that I could animate SVGs and wanted to try this out as well. For the profile icon, once the modal is open, it turns into a close icon, and I wanted to transition between the two smoothly. This involved using a tool called Flubber, which interpolates between the two icons, combined with Motion to animate the transition. Lastly, I worked on redesigning the buttons and input boxes so they match the new theme. This is the result of how the site looks so far:"}),`
